abstract: |
  The Unified Theory of Behavioral Cryptography proposes a dual-wing framework:
  the Seven-Factor Provenance Framework authenticates content origin with a joint
  forgery probability of ~10⁻⁸, while the Three-Domain Behavioral Boundary governs
  content propagation across private, community, and public domains with A0/A1/A2
  authorization codes. The two wings unite into a single mathematical model with an
  immutable Merkle propagation tree and ±5-minute responsibility attribution.
  Implementation: ~950 lines of Python (unified_boundary_engine.py).
